Body:
## Bisect result: v1.3.16 works, v1.3.17 hangs

Tested headless `opencode run` with a trivial task (read a file, return the version string):

| Version | Result |
|---------|--------|
| 1.3.15 | Completes in ~10s, exit 0 |
| 1.3.16 | Completes in ~10s, exit 0 |
| 1.3.17 | Hangs until killed (60s timeout, or indefinitely in worker dispatch) |

Only 4 commits between v1.3.16 and v1.3.17. Two are server-side (`zen:` rate limiter changes), one is Windows-only TUI. The remaining client-side change is **#20399** (Cloudflare provider env vars).

### Likely cause: unconditional `dep.auth()` in provider init

The Cloudflare provider commit moved `yield* dep.auth(input.id)` **before** the env-var fast-bail:

```ts
// v1.3.16 — fast bail, no auth call for users without Cloudflare
const accountId = Env.get("CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID")
if (!accountId) return { autoload: false }

// v1.3.17 — auth call runs for ALL users before env check
const auth = yield* dep.auth(input.id)
const accountId = Env.get("CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID") || (auth?.type === "api" ? auth.metadata?.accountId : undefined)
```

Both `cloudflare-workers-ai` and `cloudflare-ai-gateway` were also added to `INTERNAL_PLUGINS`, so they load for every user regardless of configuration. In headless mode (`opencode run`), if `dep.auth()` doesn't resolve cleanly for an unconfigured provider, it blocks provider initialization and the entire session hangs.

### Environment

- macOS (Apple Silicon)
- Headless mode via `opencode run -m anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-20250514 "..."`
- No Cloudflare env vars set (`CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`, `CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY`, etc.)
- Affects both Anthropic and OpenAI model providers (provider init blocks before model selection)

### Suggested fix

Restore the env-var fast-bail before `dep.auth()`, or skip auth for providers not configured in the user's settings:

```ts
// Check env and baseURL first — only call dep.auth() if there's reason to
if (input.options?.baseURL) return { autoload: false }
const accountId = Env.get("CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID")
if (!accountId) {
  const auth = yield* dep.auth(input.id)
  // ... check auth metadata
}
```
